Fixes for building adb with mingw-w64, from MSYS2's mingw-w64-android-tools
package (https://github.com/msys2/MINGW-packages/tree/master/mingw-w64-android-tools,
0002-android-tools-vendor.patch and 0003-fix-building-with-gcc-mingw.patch),
for android-tools 37.0.0p1. scripts/adb.sh applies it with patch -p1 to the
Windows build only. (MSYS2's 0004-leave-wstat-as-is.patch is for its newer
mingw-w64 headers; Ubuntu 24.04's need adb's own _wstat64.)

- BoringSSL: wincrypt.h's macros clash with BoringSSL's names, and its
  hand-written ADX assembly for P-256 is for the System V ABI only.
- libziparchive: mingw-w64 lays out a bit-field of uint16_t after one of
  uint32_t in a new unit, which breaks a static_assert on the struct's size.
- adb: sysdeps.h undefines write before it may be defined.

--- a/vendor/boringssl/include/openssl/target.h
+++ b/vendor/boringssl/include/openssl/target.h
@@ -78,8 +78,13 @@
 #define OPENSSL_APPLE
 #endif
 
+// Unfortunate workaround to avoid symbol conflict with wincrypt.h
+// See https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/9981
 #if defined(_WIN32)
 #define OPENSSL_WINDOWS
+#undef PKCS7_SIGNER_INFO
+#undef X509_EXTENSIONS
+#undef X509_NAME
 #endif
 
 // Trusty and Android baremetal aren't Linux but currently define __linux__.
